  "result": "Excellent! All 233 tests pass. The VAT summary feature is complete.\n\n**Summary of implementation:**\n\n**src/reports.js** \u2014 Added `vatSummary(invoices)` function that:\n- Filters invoices with status 'issued', 'partially_paid', or 'paid' (excludes draft)\n- Iterates through all lines in qualifying invoices\n- For each line, calculates:\n  - Line amount after discount: `qty * unitPrice - discount`\n  - VAT amount: `lineAmount * vatRate / 100` (rounded)\n- Groups by VAT rate and sums:\n  - `base`: total line amounts after discounts for that rate\n  - `vat`: total VAT collected at that rate\n- Returns array of `{ rate, base, vat }` entries\n- Sorted by rate descending (high to low)\n\n**test/reports.test.js** \u2014 Added 13 comprehensive VAT summary tests covering:\n- Empty arrays and filtering by status (issued/partially_paid/paid included, draft excluded)\n- Correct base and VAT calculation (with rounding)\n- Aggregation across multiple lines with same VAT rate\n- Separation of multiple VAT rates\n- Correct descending sort by rate\n- Discount and tier discount respect in base calculation\n- Aggregation across multiple invoices\n- Mixed invoice statuses\n- Type validation\n\n**Total test count: 233 passing tests** across 9 test files, covering all features:\n1. Catalogue & Customers (core infrastructure)\n2. Date handling\n3. Invoices (creation, lines, totals, discounts, VAT, vouchers)\n4. Invoice numbering\n5. Payments & balance tracking\n6. Invoice rendering\n7. Customer statements\n8. Credit notes\n9. Reports (overdue invoices, VAT summary)",
